:name: nucleus-m11-multimcu-uart-smoke
:description: Two co-simulated STM32H7 MCUs wired by a UARTHub; sender TX -> hub -> receiver RX -> relay out USART2 (captured).

# M11 inter-MCU transport DE-RISK harness (TASK-0049.01). Proves Renode
# co-simulates multiple STM32H7 machines with a WIRED inter-MCU link (a
# UARTHub — the supported cross-machine bus; Renode has no MCU-to-MCU SPI
# link). Mirrors the bundled scripts/multi-node/*.resc pattern
# (emulation CreateUARTHub + connector Connect).
#
# Caller injects three path variables before `include`-ing this script:
#   $senderBin   = @<path to the cross-compiled sender ELF>
#   $receiverBin = @<path to the cross-compiled receiver ELF>
#   $uartFile    = @<path the receiver's USART2 file backend writes to>
# (see the `renode-multimcu-uart-smoke` just recipe).

# The shared wired inter-MCU bus. Both MCUs' USART1 attach to it.
emulation CreateUARTHub "link"

mach create "sender"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl
connector Connect usart1 link

mach create "receiver"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/cpus/stm32h743.repl
connector Connect usart1 link
# Capture the receiver's relay channel (USART2 @ 0x40004400), NOT on the hub.
usart2 CreateFileBackend $uartFile true

# Fine global quantum so the two machines interleave finely (mirrors the
# bundled scripts/multi-node/*.resc, which lower the quantum for exactly
# this multi-MCU UART case).
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.00001"

mach set "sender"
sysbus LoadELF $senderBin
# START-ORDERING (load-bearing): hold the sender halted while the receiver
# boots. Renode's UARTBase.WriteChar DROPS a received char when the
# receiver's RX is not yet enabled (RE&&UE) — it does NOT queue pre-enable
# arrivals. So the sender MUST NOT transmit until the receiver has executed
# its CR1 RE-enable. Halting the sender + running the receiver alone first
# makes "receiver enables RX before sender transmits" hold BY CONSTRUCTION,
# not by scheduler luck (mirrors the nrf52840-ble-hci-uart reference, whose
# comment notes the initial bytes are dropped without this).
cpu IsHalted true

mach set "receiver"
sysbus LoadELF $receiverBin

# Let the receiver alone boot, enable USART1 RX (RE|UE) + USART2 TX, and
# enter its relay poll loop. 1ms of virtual time is ample for cortex-m-rt
# init + a few register writes; the sender is still halted here.
emulation RunFor "0.001"

# Release the sender; now it transmits into a receiver that is already
# RX-enabled and polling. Bounded run, fully determinate.
mach set "sender"
cpu IsHalted false
emulation RunFor "0.1"
quit
